            <ArticleTitle>Primary pleural chloroma: A rare location with fatal prognosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>194-196</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1759-7714.2011.00068.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report an extremely unique histologically proven case of an isolated primary pleural granulocytic sarcoma (chloroma) in a 44-year-old woman who had sustained complete remission for 14 years after being treated for a Hodgkin's lymphoma. There was no history of myelogenous leukemia, which typically precedes chloroma. The prognosis was dismal as the patient died 2 weeks after diagnosis.</AbstractText>
